{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"22179175-7479-4d9d-acbb-427d0e643097","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A derivative measures a curve’s slope at one point. Start with this parabola and the point where x equals one.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Derivative = tangent slope"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,2.4],"y":[-0.5,5.5],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"curve","y":"x^2","domain":[0,2.3],"label":"y = x²"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":{"on":"curve","x":1},"label":"P (1, 1)"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"function","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f(x)=x^2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"22179175-7479-4d9d-acbb-427d0e643097","step":{"id":"s2","script":"A second point gives a secant line. Its slope is the change in height divided by the change in horizontal position.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"secant","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"q","at":{"on":"curve","x":2},"label":"Q (2, 4)"},{"kind":"segment","id":"pq","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":[2,1],"stroke":"dashed","label":"Δx = 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,1],"to":{"at":"q"},"stroke":"dashed","label":"Δy = 3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"secantslope","anchor":{"el":"function","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"m_{\\text{sec}}=\\frac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}=2+h"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"22179175-7479-4d9d-acbb-427d0e643097","step":{"id":"s3","script":"As the second point approaches P, h approaches zero. The secant slope approaches two, giving the tangent’s slope at P.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"tangentink","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"tangent","id":"tangent","to":"curve","x":1,"length":0.85,"label":"tangent"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"curve","x":1.3}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"on":"curve","x":1.3},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"limit","anchor":{"el":"secantslope","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f'(1)=\\lim_{h\\to0}(2+h)=2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Is the derivative at P the slope of the curve’s tangent or the height of P?","expected_gist":"The tangent slope, which is 2."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"22179175-7479-4d9d-acbb-427d0e643097","step":{"id":"s4","script":"On the tangent, a horizontal run of one gives a rise of two. The derivative is two, not the point’s height of one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"slopetriangle","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"p"},"to":[2,1],"label":"run 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,1],"to":[2,3],"label":"rise 2"},{"kind":"point","at":[2,3]}]},{"op":"equation","id":"tangenteq","anchor":{"el":"limit","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y-1=2(x-1)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
